<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Consell de Cent</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1265">1265</a>–<a href="/years/1714">1714</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Council of One Hundred</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Consell de Cent ('Council of One Hundred') was the governing council of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> from the 1260s until 1714. Representing citizens, merchants and craftsmen, it ran the city's finances and defence and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taula-de-canvi">Taula de Canvi</a> in 1401; it was abolished by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta decrees</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/consell-de-cent.jpg" alt="Consell de Cent" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oliver-Bonjoch · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salo_de_Cent.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
